# p_e7b3 — The Living Room Reset; Blanket on Armchair, Remote on Floor, Water at Dining Table

A fresh document correcting the resting positions of several living-room and dining-room objects that the existing library consistently misplaces. The per-object evidence and clock-hour sightings show: the shared blanket lives on armchair_l1 (sighted there 00:00–10:00 every weekday, only at coffee_table_l1 at 18:00 and 22:00); the remote lives on floor_l_l1 (sighted there 00:00–10:00, only at tv_stand_l1 at 18:00–20:00 and coffee_table_l1 at 22:00); Priya's water bottle lives at dining_table_d1 (sighted there 00:00–12:00 and 20:00–22:00, only at coffee_table_l1 at 18:00); Priya's plate lives at dining_table_d1 (sighted there 00:00–12:00 and 20:00–22:00, only at cupboard_k1 at 18:00); and Priya's shoes live at entry_floor_e1 (sighted there 00:00–06:00, 12:00, 20:00–22:00, only at shoe_rack_e1 at 08:00 and 18:00).

The interpretation: these objects are left out in their "in-use" or "convenient" positions and are only briefly stowed during a mid-afternoon tidy-up (around 17:00–19:00). The blanket is draped over the armchair where someone was sitting; the remote was dropped on the floor during TV and never picked up; Priya's water bottle and plate stay at the dining table where she eats; her shoes stay by the door rather than on the rack.

What sets this apart: blanket at armchair_l1 (not coffee_table_l1) overnight; remote at floor_l_l1 (not tv_stand_l1) overnight; water_bottle_priya at dining_table_d1 (not coffee_table_l1) overnight; plate_priya at dining_table_d1 (not cupboard_k1) overnight. What would refute it: blanket_shared found at coffee_table_l1 at 02:00; remote_shared found at tv_stand_l1 at 04:00; water_bottle_priya found at coffee_table_l1 at 02:00.

